# Build-context exclusions for the app images (api / worker).
#
# Must be passed explicitly: `podman build --ignorefile deploy/app/.dockerignore ...` because the build
# context is the repository root and this file does not live there. With it missing, `apps/` alone pushed
# ~1 GB of Docusaurus build output and node_modules into the context and `COPY . .` appeared to hang.
.git
.github
.vscode
.dsh
.kilo
.tools
skills
docs
**/node_modules
node_modules
apps
.playwright-mcp
**/.wrangler
packages/workers/.wrangler
**/.docusaurus
**/build
**/dist
**/coverage
*.log
*.tar
*.tsbuildinfo
build-api.log
build-edge.log

# Every .env, not just the root one: COPY . . otherwise bakes packages/server/.env into the image and
# load-env injects it at startup (observed: 'injected env (9) from .env'), which both leaks
# credentials into the image and lets stale localhost URLs shadow the cluster Secret.
**/.env
.env*
!.env.example
